1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,812
<font color="#000000">InfinityGAN asks a bold question: can a model
synthesize images of arbitrary,</font>

2
00:00:05,892 --> 00:00:11,553
<font color="#000000">even infinite size, while training only on small
patches on a single consumer GPU?</font>

3
00:00:11,633 --> 00:00:15,684
<font color="#000000">Existing high-resolution GANs fail because compute,
memory,</font>

4
00:00:15,764 --> 00:00:18,625
<font color="#000000">and data all scale with output resolution.</font>

5
00:00:18,705 --> 00:00:24,227
<font color="#000000">InfinityGAN breaks that coupling, disentangling an
image into global appearance,</font>

6
00:00:24,307 --> 00:00:26,608
<font color="#000000">local structure, and fine texture,</font>

7
00:00:26,688 --> 00:00:32,139
<font color="#000000">and generating any region patch-by-patch from
continuous coordinates, seamless,</font>

8
00:00:32,219 --> 00:00:35,150
<font color="#000000">globally consistent, and unbounded in size.</font>

9
00:00:35,530 --> 00:00:39,332
<font color="#000000">Modern generative models keep improving in
resolution and detail,</font>

10
00:00:39,412 --> 00:00:43,215
<font color="#000000">but every gain costs more training time, a bigger model,</font>

11
00:00:43,295 --> 00:00:47,097
<font color="#000000">and large field-of-view images that are hard to collect.</font>

12
00:00:47,177 --> 00:00:50,980
<font color="#000000">Worse, existing generators are locked to their
training resolution.</font>

13
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:54,862
<font color="#000000">Push them larger,</font>

14
00:00:54,942 --> 00:00:58,745
<font color="#000000">and compute and memory explode quadratically while
global structure falls apart.</font>

15
00:00:58,825 --> 00:01:02,627
<font color="#000000">InfinityGAN asks how to escape this coupling and
synthesize arbitrary,</font>

16
00:01:02,707 --> 00:01:06,510
<font color="#000000">even infinite images from finite data on modest hardware.</font>

17
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:10,021
<font color="#000000">Why do existing models fail when asked to grow?</font>

18
00:01:10,101 --> 00:01:17,057
<font color="#000000">The insight: generators like StyleGAN2 secretly
rely on zero-padding at the borders to encode position.</font>

19
00:01:17,137 --> 00:01:22,112
<font color="#000000">During training the padding pattern is fixed, so
the network memorizes it.</font>

20
00:01:22,192 --> 00:01:26,211
<font color="#000000">But synthesize a larger image, and the feature size
changes,</font>

21
00:01:26,291 --> 00:01:28,670
<font color="#000000">the padding-derived position shifts,</font>

22
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:33,315
<font color="#000000">and the image center no longer gets sensible
positional information,</font>

23
00:01:33,395 --> 00:01:35,842
<font color="#000000">producing repetitive, broken content.</font>

24
00:01:35,922 --> 00:01:41,102
<font color="#000000">Truly infinite synthesis needs position valid
infinitely far from any border,</font>

25
00:01:41,182 --> 00:01:43,630
<font color="#000000">plus patches that combine seamlessly.</font>

26
00:01:44,010 --> 00:01:48,185
<font color="#000000">InfinityGAN makes five contributions.</font>

27
00:01:48,265 --> 00:01:52,440
<font color="#000000">First, it reframes generation as disentangling
global appearance, local structure,</font>

28
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:56,695
<font color="#000000">and fine texture, each with a dedicated component.</font>

29
00:01:56,775 --> 00:02:00,950
<font color="#000000">Second,</font>

30
00:02:01,030 --> 00:02:05,205
<font color="#000000">a structure synthesizer built as a neural implicit
function driven by continuous coordinates,</font>

31
00:02:05,285 --> 00:02:09,460
<font color="#000000">so any sub-region can be queried directly.</font>

32
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:13,715
<font color="#000000">Third, a padding-free generator removing all zero-padding,</font>

33
00:02:13,795 --> 00:02:17,970
<font color="#000000">letting patches synthesize independently yet
combine seamlessly.</font>

34
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:22,225
<font color="#000000">Fourth, a scale-invariant FID metric for sizes
where no real reference images exist.</font>

35
00:02:22,305 --> 00:02:26,480
<font color="#000000">Finally, applications the design unlocks, from
spatial style fusion to outpainting.</font>

36
00:02:26,860 --> 00:02:29,459
<font color="#000000">InfinityGAN's generator has two modules.</font>

37
00:02:29,539 --> 00:02:36,357
<font color="#000000">The structure synthesizer is a neural implicit
function: it takes a global latent for scene appearance,</font>

38
00:02:36,437 --> 00:02:41,045
<font color="#000000">a local latent tensor for variation, and a
continuous coordinate grid,</font>

39
00:02:41,125 --> 00:02:44,192
<font color="#000000">and outputs a structural latent for any region.</font>

40
00:02:44,272 --> 00:02:50,085
<font color="#000000">Coordinates use sine-cosine horizontally to exploit
landscape self-similarity and a tanh</font>

41
00:02:50,165 --> 00:02:52,898
<font color="#000000">vertically for the ground-to-sky gradient,</font>

42
00:02:52,978 --> 00:02:56,381
<font color="#000000">so it can be queried infinitely far from the origin.</font>

43
00:02:56,461 --> 00:03:02,341
<font color="#000000">The texture synthesizer is a fully-convolutional
StyleGAN2 with all zero-padding removed,</font>

44
00:03:02,421 --> 00:03:06,895
<font color="#000000">turning the structural latent, global style, and
noise into a patch.</font>

45
00:03:06,975 --> 00:03:11,449
<font color="#000000">With no padding, the same coordinate always yields
identical pixels,</font>

46
00:03:11,529 --> 00:03:15,333
<font color="#000000">so independent patches tile seamlessly at constant memory.</font>

47
00:03:15,413 --> 00:03:19,217
<font color="#000000">Training combines adversarial, R1, path-length, diversity,</font>

48
00:03:19,297 --> 00:03:22,030
<font color="#000000">and vertical-coordinate regression losses.</font>

49
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:25,129
<font color="#000000">The authors introduce Flickr-Landscape,</font>

50
00:03:25,209 --> 00:03:30,728
<font color="#000000">four hundred fifty thousand high-quality landscape
images crawled from Flickr,</font>

51
00:03:30,808 --> 00:03:33,599
<font color="#000000">to evaluate synthesis at extended sizes.</font>

52
00:03:33,679 --> 00:03:37,475
<font color="#000000">For outpainting they use scenery subsets of Places365,</font>

53
00:03:37,555 --> 00:03:41,710
<font color="#000000">sixty-two thousand five hundred images, and
Flickr-Scenery,</font>

54
00:03:41,790 --> 00:03:43,576
<font color="#000000">about fifty-four thousand.</font>

55
00:03:43,656 --> 00:03:49,390
<font color="#000000">Remarkably, every InfinityGAN model trains on tiny
one-hundred-one-pixel patches,</font>

56
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:54,630
<font color="#000000">and both training and any-size inference run on a
single GTX TITAN X GPU.</font>

57
00:03:55,010 --> 00:03:57,268
<font color="#000000">On the Flickr-Landscape benchmark,</font>

58
00:03:57,348 --> 00:04:01,189
<font color="#000000">InfinityGAN holds a steady quality slope as output grows,</font>

59
00:04:01,269 --> 00:04:04,696
<font color="#000000">while baselines drift far from realistic structure.</font>

60
00:04:04,776 --> 00:04:08,823
<font color="#000000">Beyond four-times extension it beats the strongest
baseline,</font>

61
00:04:08,903 --> 00:04:16,664
<font color="#000000">scoring a scale-invariant FID of sixty-one point
four at four-times versus seventy-nine point eight for StyleGAN2,</font>

62
00:04:16,744 --> 00:04:20,584
<font color="#000000">and one twenty-one versus one eighty-nine at eight-times.</font>

63
00:04:20,664 --> 00:04:26,017
<font color="#000000">Its memory stays constant, while StyleGAN2 runs out
of memory at sixteen-times.</font>

64
00:04:26,097 --> 00:04:29,800
<font color="#000000">And over ninety percent preferred it over every method.</font>

65
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:34,702
<font color="#000000">The central ablation isolates where positional
information comes from.</font>

66
00:04:34,782 --> 00:04:37,858
<font color="#000000">Starting from StyleGAN2 with non-constant input,</font>

67
00:04:37,938 --> 00:04:40,422
<font color="#000000">the authors strip out all zero-padding,</font>

68
00:04:40,502 --> 00:04:44,104
<font color="#000000">creating a padding-free variant with no positional cues.</font>

69
00:04:44,184 --> 00:04:49,890
<font color="#000000">It fails to generate reasonable structure and
degrades sharply across every FID setting,</font>

70
00:04:49,970 --> 00:04:54,755
<font color="#000000">confirming the original generator leaned entirely
on padding for position.</font>

71
00:04:54,835 --> 00:04:57,056
<font color="#000000">Add the structure synthesizer back,</font>

72
00:04:57,136 --> 00:05:02,119
<font color="#000000">and position is now supplied through the
coordinate-driven structural latent,</font>

73
00:05:02,199 --> 00:05:04,880
<font color="#000000">so quality returns, validating the design.</font>

74
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:12,159
<font color="#000000">The headline numbers: scale-invariant FID of
sixty-one at four-times and one twenty-one at eight-times,</font>

75
00:05:12,239 --> 00:05:14,598
<font color="#000000">both beating the strongest baseline.</font>

76
00:05:14,678 --> 00:05:17,105
<font color="#000000">Over ninety percent human preference.</font>

77
00:05:17,185 --> 00:05:21,916
<font color="#000000">Up to seven point two times faster inference
through parallel batching,</font>

78
00:05:21,996 --> 00:05:27,946
<font color="#000000">cutting eight-thousand-pixel synthesis from one
hundred thirty-seven seconds to nineteen.</font>

79
00:05:28,026 --> 00:05:30,588
<font color="#000000">Paired with In-and-Out for outpainting,</font>

80
00:05:30,668 --> 00:05:36,280
<font color="#000000">FID drops to nine on Places365 and fifteen on
Flickr-Scenery, halving previous best.</font>

81
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:43,915
<font color="#FFFFFF">The takeaway: infinite-pixel synthesis becomes
tractable once you stop tying generation to a fixed resolution.</font>

82
00:05:43,995 --> 00:05:46,049
<font color="#FFFFFF">By separating global appearance,</font>

83
00:05:46,129 --> 00:05:49,917
<font color="#FFFFFF">local structure via a coordinate-driven implicit function,</font>

84
00:05:49,997 --> 00:05:52,651
<font color="#FFFFFF">and texture via a padding-free generator,</font>

85
00:05:52,731 --> 00:05:57,653
<font color="#FFFFFF">InfinityGAN produces patches that are independent
yet perfectly consistent,</font>

86
00:05:57,733 --> 00:06:02,721
<font color="#FFFFFF">tiling into images of any size at constant memory
and generated in parallel.</font>

87
00:06:02,801 --> 00:06:07,589
<font color="#FFFFFF">The same framework unlocks spatial style fusion,
multi-modal outpainting,</font>

88
00:06:07,669 --> 00:06:11,190
<font color="#FFFFFF">and arbitrary-length panoramas, all from tiny patches.</font>
